   "canonical_url": "https://sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/11/261109205401.htm",
   "title": "Obesity linked to up to 27% lower risk of death in dementia",
   "snippet": "A surprising study of more than 4,500 older adults found that people who were overweight or obese when diagnosed with dementia had a 16% to 27% lower risk of death than those at a normal weight. Researchers suspect that extra energy and muscle reserves may help patients survive the disease's toll on the body, although the reason for the survival advantage remains unclear.",
